# =====================================================================
# Release V100 -- FTE moves from Practitioner_Pay to Practitioner_Role (Roles screen)
# =====================================================================
# FTE is a per-practitioner allocation like the role, so it now lives with Custom_Role in
# Input.Practitioner_Role and is edited on the Roles screen (not the Finance/Associate-Pay screen).
# Deploy in sequence AFTER V099. Idempotent: table DDL DROP/CREATE (sync target), SPs CREATE.
# Run: .\Scripts\Deploy.ps1 -Manifest Releases\V100__fte_moves_to_role.manifest -SkipTests
#
# Warehouse changes:
#   * Input.Practitioner_Role -> +FTE column (recreate; it is a sync target, repopulated from AppDB).
#   * Meta.usp_Sync_Input_From_AppDB -> Practitioner_Role copy now carries FTE.
#   * Gold.usp_Load_Dim_Practitioners -> FTE sourced from Input.Practitioner_Role (was Practitioner_Pay).
#     Practitioner_Pay.FTE is left in place but unused (Finance screen keeps Associate_Pct only).
#
# OUT-OF-BAND (do first / alongside):
#   1. PROD AppDB: re-run AppDB\AppDB_Input_Schema.sql -- the guarded ALTER adds FTE to
#      Input.Practitioner_Role on an already-provisioned DB. Allow a few minutes for OneLake
#      mirroring before the sync (the new COLUMN mirrors like a new table did).
#   2. APP: the Roles screen now has the FTE input; the Finance screen drops it (rides the app PR).
#   3. If FTE was already entered on the Finance screen into Practitioner_Pay, migrate it once:
#        UPDATE r SET r.FTE = pp.FTE FROM Input.Practitioner_Role r
#        JOIN Input.Practitioner_Pay pp ON pp.Tenant_ID=r.Tenant_ID AND pp.Practitioner_ID=r.Practitioner_ID
#        WHERE pp.FTE IS NOT NULL;   -- run in AppDB, then it syncs through on the next build.
# =====================================================================

DEPLOY   Fabric\Input.Practitioner_Role.Table.sql
DEPLOY   Fabric\Meta.usp_Sync_Input_From_AppDB.StoredProcedure.sql
DEPLOY   Fabric\Gold.usp_Load_Dim_Practitioners.StoredProcedure.sql

TEST
